<mjml>
<!--
  IMPECCABLE DIRECTION CONTRACT
  THESIS: this is a status update, not a moment to celebrate — the customer
  just wants three facts fast (whose order, what number, what happens next)
  and a way to check on it. Amber is the hero band's fill specifically
  because DESIGN.md documents Amber as the "pending/status accent" — this is
  the one email in the redesigned set that's genuinely still pending
  something (the distributor's acceptance), so the color itself carries
  meaning, differentiating this at a glance from Order Confirmed's blue band
  once both land in the same inbox.
  OWN-WORLD: apps/portal/DESIGN.md, inherited from invite.mjml exactly —
  same header/footer chrome (partials/_header.mjml, _footer.mjml), same
  hard 0px corners / flat hairline card frame (E6ECF2, unchanged regardless
  of a band's fill color — the frame is the one constant across every email
  in this set), same floated-circle distributor-identity technique.
  STORY: a customer who just placed an order sees it landed with the right
  distributor, has something to reference (order number), knows they're not
  done waiting yet, and can go look at it if they want to.
  FIRST VIEWPORT: header, then one amber band — headline, distributor
  identity + order number, a status note, a "View order" CTA (omitted
  gracefully if no portal link is available) — then straight to the footer.
  No benefits list, no second content section: there's nothing else this
  email needs to say, and padding it out would be filler, not information.
  FORM: extends the established invite.mjml world onto a second, structurally
  simpler surface — no concept-seed tournament, direction was already set.
  FINISH: verified via a real MJML render/screenshot + a real MailHog send,
  same bar as invite.mjml.
-->
<mj-head>
  <mj-title>Your order with {{distributorName}} has been received</mj-title>
  <mj-font name="Inter" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  <mj-attributes>
    <mj-text font-size="14px" font-weight="400" line-height="1.5" color="#0B1D3A" padding="0" />
  </mj-attributes>
  <mj-style>
    @media only screen and (max-width:480px) {
      .distributor-byline-logo {
        width: 44px !important;
        height: 44px !important;
        border-radius: 23px !important;
      }
    }
  </mj-style>
</mj-head>
<mj-body background-color="#F2F4F7" width="480px">

  {{> header}}

  <!-- Hero band: Amber fill (#FEEFE7, DESIGN.md's amber-light tint) marks
       the pending wait state. Identity mark floats beside the first
       sentence exactly as in invite.mjml (same technique, same graceful
       degradation with no logo). Order number and next-step status share
       one Slate Blue line — two related facts, not two separate paragraphs. -->
  <!-- Section's own bottom padding (32px, a fixed card-edge close) rather
       than relying on the last element's padding-bottom for the closing
       edge — the CTA below is conditional (omitted with no portal link),
       so the "last element" isn't always the same one; a section-level
       fixed edge keeps the band's close consistent either way. -->
  <mj-section background-color="#FEEFE7" padding="32px 32px 32px" border-left="1px solid #E6ECF2" border-right="1px solid #E6ECF2">
    <mj-column>
      <mj-text font-size="24px" font-weight="600" line-height="1.3" color="#0B1D3A" padding-bottom="16px">
        Order received
      </mj-text>
      {{> identity-row}}
      <mj-text color="#5B6B7F" padding-bottom="24px">
        Order number <strong style="color:#0B1D3A;">{{orderNumber}}</strong>. You'll get another email as soon as {{distributorName}} accepts it.
      </mj-text>
      {{#if orderUrl}}
      <mj-button href="{{orderUrl}}" background-color="#1565FF" color="#FFFFFF" font-size="15px"
        font-weight="600" border-radius="0" padding="0" inner-padding="14px 32px" align="center">
        View order
      </mj-button>
      {{/if}}
    </mj-column>
  </mj-section>

  {{> footer}}

</mj-body>
</mjml>
